reagent-name-heroin = heroin
reagent-desc-heroin = A refined opiate, commonly injected as a means of reducing pain. Overdose is incredibly deadly

reagent-name-opium = opium
reagent-desc-opium = unrefined opium, the milk of the poppy. Once used as a analgesic in surgery, now used as a catalyst to make stronger medications.

reagent-name-pcp = 14-SPCeM-E3NS-PCP
reagent-desc-pcp = An incredibly strong dissociative hallucinogen. Due to its chemical structure this can only be taken orally, or injected. While it is not lethal, large doses tend to lead to psychosis or mania.
